    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense faces a mixed slate today, headlined by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Jacob Wilson** (73.48), who represent our most efficient starts. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against Yesavage, where a +11% SP skill adjustment and a dynamic platoon advantage propel his ceiling. Similarly, **Jacob Wilson** is locked into the leadoff spot against a volatile arm in Patrick Sandoval; his combination of order-based upside and a +10% park factor makes him a core pillar of today\u2019s production. **Curtis Mead** (60.34) also earns a high-confidence start, capitalizing on a strong SP skill projection against Jacob Lopez to push comfortably into the 60+ efficiency bracket.\n\nThe bench decision for **Gunnar Henderson** (46.70) highlights our strict commitment to daily efficiency, as he sits despite his high base projection. While **Gunnar Henderson** remains a staple of our roster, the combination of a daunting matchup against Skubal and a negative platoon split pushed his projected efficiency below our active threshold, opening the door for players with more favorable situational matchups. Elsewhere, we must monitor the high-risk entries: **Drake Baldwin**, **Jorge Polanco**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** all carry a 45% rain risk. **Luis Robert Jr.** is of particular concern, as his 51.83 score is already pressured by the elite presence of Chris Sale on the mound; any delay or cancellation could significantly hinder our ability to reach our aggregate scoring targets. \n\nWe are leaning into the speed element today, with **Nasim Nunez** (57.81) and **Andy Pages** (58.95) providing steady floors. **Andy Pages** is especially intriguing, as the slow delivery of Emerson Hancock offers a subtle uptick in his stolen base potential\u2014a critical factor given our league's scarcity-driven focus. While **Kyle Tucker** (59.56) and **Jackson Merrill** (59.31) fall just shy of the \"Strong\" 60+ threshold, their dynamic platoon matchups against Right-handed starters keep them as essential components of our pursuit of volume in the HR and RBI categories.",
